      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Modifying an asset currently requires grabbing a mutable reference to `Assets<T>`. This makes sense conceptually, but Legion's Scheduler (correctly) synchronizes when a mutable reference is grabbed. This means multiple systems requiring mut access to the same `Assets<T>` storage cant run in parallel.\r\n\r\nIt is worth adding some interior mutability / `RwLock`s to `Assets<T>` to see if this improves performance for common use cases.",
